Validation: gzip kernel sections with appended DTBs
Repository: https://github.com/samcday/pocketboot
Commit: 543612bb4f5000848939bca97dafb2937993cf4f
Sole parent/base: 79cdf784c476be70f7f58cd73b37dfaeb0bf1c6f (main)
No Ferrari configuration, CPU-parking or boot-menu change in this PR.

Root cause reproduced before this fix on CI parking artifact36504432549: flate2=1.1.9 MultiGzDecoder reports InvalidInput "invalid gzip header" after decoding12779520 bytes, because the next48897 bytes are an FDT, not another gzip member. The first member's CRC/footer is valid. The kernel section contains5083892 bytes.

Fix: single-member BufRead gzip decoding in a loop retains member boundaries and validates every gzip member. Only one immediately appended v17-format-compatible FDT (optional zero trailing padding) is accepted. Header/block bounds, alignment/overlap, terminated reserve map and full tree structure are checked; unknown bytes/multiple DTBs/structural junk after FDT_END are rejected. Kernel preparation lives in KexecImage::new so both existing callers use explicit DTB > appended DTB > live fallback. Explicit DTBs do not excuse malformed kernel trailers. Raw/PE/zboot behavior is otherwise preserved; raw Image+DTB splitting is not added.

