To reproduce the real-artifact check after independent extraction:
POCKETBOOT_TEST_BOOT_IMAGE=<boot.img> POCKETBOOT_TEST_KERNEL=<decompressed-kernel> POCKETBOOT_TEST_DTB=<appended.dtb> cargo test --locked --offline -p pocketboot inspect_supplied_android_image -- --ignored --nocapture
For ARM64, add --target aarch64-unknown-linux-musl and CARGO_TARGET_AARCH64_UNKNOWN_LINUX_MUSL_RUNNER=qemu-aarch64.

Regression tests also cover synthetic Androidv0 gzip+DTB, the complete padded preboot envelope/inner BSS, Androidv2 explicit-DTB precedence, plain gzip/live fallback, multi-member gzip, bad CRC/ISIZE, truncation, bad FDT bounds/version/structure/reservation maps, multiple trees and trailing garbage. Independent review found no constructor/caller/member-boundary regression and identified the post-FDT_END check, which was added and tested before final validation.

Limits: all checks are host parsing/compile or user-mode emulation. No phone, flashing, real kernel handoff or direct-OEM boot. A running pocketboot must contain this fix to parse these images; changing only the image being uploaded to an old pocketboot does not fix its decoder. Direct-OEM hardware work remains opt-in with pem120; request posted at https://github.com/pem120/linux/issues/3#issuecomment-5902266159 .
